# Globs are fnmatch, not gitignore syntax: `*` crosses `/`.
#
# The tests use version literals (py39, 3.11.9, "Python 3.13+") as fixture data.
# Without this entry, every minor bump fails on the test suite's own fixtures.
#
# README.md is deliberately NOT listed. It documents rules using the current
# version, so the hook keeps its own documentation honest on the next bump --
# which is the whole argument for the prose rules.
tests/*

# Toolchain definitions are regexes and form templates. They cite token shapes
# (`python3.9`, `py39`) as illustrations of what a rule matches, and never carry
# a version this repo runs on -- so there is nothing in them that *could* drift.
# Scoped to this directory rather than all of src/, where a hardcoded version
# would be a genuine bug.
src/version_drift/toolchains/*
